<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Color tokens from DESIGN.md (and its sidecar .impeccable/design.json): the only place literal colors may live.

  Every token is a Color (<Name>Color) and a SolidColorBrush (<Name>Brush) in each of the Light, Dark
  and HighContrast theme dictionaries, so a control looks up one key and gets the value for the current
  theme. HighContrast maps to Windows system colors and has no amber (DESIGN.md Overview; Color canvas,
  high contrast table). Keys not tied to a theme (letterbox, the day-to-night ramp) sit at the root.
  Control-level overrides that use these are in ControlOverrides.xaml.

  Keys follow the DESIGN.md token names in PascalCase: golden-hour-amber is GoldenHourAmberColor and
  GoldenHourAmberBrush; the "-light" and "-dark" variants are the same key in the Light and Dark dictionaries.

  Amber rule: GoldenHourAmber* is the fill of the one accent button per screen (DESIGN.md): ExportButtonStyle,
  and AccentActionButtonStyle on a screen without Export (Choose folder). DeepAmberIndicator* is the state
  indicator (progress, scrubber, playhead ring, toggles that are on, selection). Never use GoldenHourAmber for
  an indicator in the light theme (2.26:1 on the layer).

  DeepAmberIndicatorHover and DeepAmberIndicatorPressed are the indicator's hover and press feedback, taken
  from its tonal ramp in .impeccable/design.json: Light steps lighter on hover (#BD6A1D) and darker on press
  (#924C00); Dark is the inverse (#DD9155 on hover, #FDB885 on press). Each keeps 3:1 against Track and Mica.
  HighContrast uses Hotlight for both, so hover and press differ from the Highlight rest state.
-->
<ResourceDictionary
  xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
